### Designer — 10 goals
*theme: from one-off fixes to a repeatable design system with a quality gate*
1. Full design token layer - extend --sp-*/--fs-* into a complete token set (color, radius, shadow, motion-duration) as CSS custom properties; documented in memory/portal/design-tokens-live.md (extends the ui-tokens.md lineage). Verified: grep confirms every hard-coded color/radius/duration replaced by var(--token); file index-linked.
2. Dark mode + theme toggle - persistent light/dark driven by the token layer, header toggle, prefers-color-scheme fallback; no contrast regressions in either mode. Verified: screenshot pair on :8099; WCAG AA script re-run on both themes, 0 failures.
3. Component abstraction - extract .msg / .panel-head / .btn-primary / .badge-status / .input-bar as named classes; eliminate inline style= attributes from chat and panel elements. Verified: grep shows zero style= on those selectors; HTML line count drops >=20%.
4. Micro-interactions & motion budget - CSS transitions on panel expand/collapse, message hover, button press; all <=200ms; respect prefers-reduced-motion. Verified: computed transition-duration grep max 200ms + manual interaction pass with before/after.
5. Breakpoint regression automation (replaces the original <768px responsive goal - already shipped 2026-11-16) - turn d7_d9_cdp_verify.py into a scheduled design_breakpoint_check.py: screenshots at 375/768 + assert 0 console errors + 0 horizontal overflow; wired as a pre-deploy gate. Verified by forcing a layout break (overflow) -> check fails with screenshot evidence.
6. Status indicator system - consistent .status-dot component (green/amber/red + label) across Fleet panel, Ops git status, and agent roster; replaces ad-hoc colored text. Verified: grep confirms .status-dot in all three panels; no bare color:green/red remains.
7. Focus rings + ARIA landmarks - visible 2px offset focus ring on every interactive element; panels wrapped in <section aria-label>; nav landmarks for screen readers. Verified: axe/Lighthouse accessibility score >=95 on :8099; tab-through shows no invisible focus.
8. Typography hierarchy pass - line-height 1.2-1.6 (headings vs body), +0.05em letter-spacing on uppercase labels, >=3 meaningful font-weight steps; no element outside range. Verified: computed-style dump script confirms zero violations + visual before/after of a dense panel.
9. Live fleet topology view - SVG diagram of 3 hosts + agent nodes from /api/net/fleet (data source: Mechanic#8 endpoint); hover tooltips, click-to-expand detail card, live status color sync. Verified: screenshot with all 3 hosts rendered at correct status after API poll; console clean.
10. Design QA regression gate - design-check.py greps CSS for token violations, contrast failures, missing focus styles; pre-deploy step reporting pass/fail; referenced in the TODO deploy runbook. Verified: script runs against current CSS -> 0 violations; a deliberate violation is caught and named.

### Mechanic — 10 goals
*theme: from reactive monitoring to proactive self-healing, machine-readable evidence*
1. Adaptive fleet probe - upgrade fleet_probe.py from fixed 10-min cadence to trend-aware: latency drift and process-count anomalies across consecutive runs escalate severity before hard failure; WARN/CRIT levels logged to memory/ops/probe-evidence.jsonl. Verified: simulating a degrading host -> severity escalates over N runs.
2. Full reboot-recovery automation (all 4 legs) - complete Pale/Black/Red dry-runs (White done), wire into a boot-detection scheduled task that auto-executes recovery; <60s from power-on to portal serving on every host. Verified: one real cold-boot test per remote with timestamped evidence.
3. Self-healing SMB mirror - extend sync verification to auto-repair: missed-sync detection triggers re-sync automatically + repair event logged with timestamp; zero human intervention for single-leg failures, only multi-leg cascades escalate. Verified: killing one leg mid-sync -> auto re-sync within 5 min, logged.
4. Portal load test & capacity baseline (SLO pipeline, Mechanic role) - daily probe of concurrent requests against :8099 (10/50/200); p50/p95/p99 per endpoint into memory/ops/load-baseline.jsonl; trend so regressions surface before users notice. Feeds Builder#8 + Verifier#4. Verified: one week of baseline data with a regression demo caught.
5. Change-entity health integration - probe output wired into the evolution layer: host down or critical port dead auto-creates a CHG entity (status=born) so outages are trackable alongside CHG-0001/CHG-0002. Verified: forcing a probe failure -> CHG entity appears with correct fields.
6. Netcmd egress guard -> rules engine - extend the allow_public 403 to per-host/per-port/per-domain allowlists with structured audit log; any non-allowlisted outbound blocked + logged with one-line reason (memory/ops/egress-audit.jsonl). Verified: matrix of allowed/blocked probes with raw logs.
7. Scheduled-task dependency graph - textual blast-radius map of all schtasks across 4 hosts ("if PortalDailyGitCommit fails, what else breaks?"); every critical task documented. Verified: memory/ops/schtask-deps.md covers 100% of tasks in `schtasks /query`.
8. Fleet health dashboard endpoint - GET /api/health/fleet in agent_portal.py: per-host status, port checks, last probe time, SMB sync age, git commit freshness in one JSON; single call = full fleet picture. Feeds Builder#6 parity guard + Designer#9 topology view. Verified: one call returns all 4 hosts with fresh timestamps; a downed host flagged correctly.
9. Weekly chaos drill (rotating host) - scheduled task kills the portal process on one host per week (White->Pale->Black->Red rotation), verifies auto-restart within 5 min, logs pass/fail. Verified: first drill executed + logged during cycle 2.
10. Ops knowledge-base consolidation - consolidate scattered runbooks, probe scripts and evidence into a single searchable memory/ops/ with INDEX.md; every fix gets a one-line entry. Verified: new agent onboards to fleet ops in <10 min by reading the index alone (timed dry-run).

### Archivist — 10 goals
*theme: from checking knowledge to growing, predicting and ingesting it*
1. Knowledge graph & lineage tracker - `archivist/knowledge_graph.py` walks all memory leaves, extracts cross-references (pointers, see-also, supersession markers) -> JSON dependency graph + rendered text view; flags circular references and orphaned nodes. Verified: first run reports N nodes / M edges with zero unexplained orphans vs the index_check baseline.
2. Freshness SLA monitor - extend index_check into `memory_health.py`: per-leaf staleness against declared TTLs (ops runbooks <=14d, architecture <=30d, goals = cycle length); auto freshness-report.md; non-zero exit on breach; GET /api/memory/health endpoint. Verified: seeding a stale leaf -> endpoint reports it + gate fails.
3. Cross-agent knowledge handoff protocol - memory/handoffs/PROTOCOL.md (trigger conditions, provenance-header template, acceptance criteria, index update) + one real handoff processed end-to-end and logged in LOG.md. Verified: handoff complete with both parties' sign-off lines.
4. Auto-generated API reference - `archivist/gen_api_ref.py` parses route definitions from agent_portal.py -> memory/portal/api-reference.md; pre-prune gate fails if generated doc differs from committed. Verified: adding a dummy route -> gate fails until the doc is regenerated.
5. Supersession chain validator (script owner per charter) - `archivist/supersession_check.py` finds all supersession markers ("supersedes", "replaced by"), validates chains are acyclic and terminate at a living leaf, flags orphaned superseded files eligible for archival; Scribe#5 consumes the report for policy + weekly runs. Verified: baseline run reports every chain + any broken links.
6. Multi-host documentation consistency check - extract host-specific factual claims from memory/ops/ + portal/architecture.md ("endpoint X exists on Red/Pale/Black", "file Y at path Z"); verify each via fleet API or direct probes; report discrepancies. Verified: first report with per-claim pass/fail.
7. Knowledge decay model & weekly review - `archivist/decay_score.py` scores every leaf on recency x reference density x index-linkage; composite below threshold -> flagged for review/archival; weekly decay-report.md. Verified: first weekly run produces a ranked flag list.
8. Agent onboarding knowledge pack - memory/ONBOARDING.md readable in <15 min (tree structure, conventions, where-to-find-what); skeleton auto-generated from INDEX.md and regenerated on index change. Verified: a new agent or human locates 5 named facts using only the pack.
9. Versioned knowledge snapshots & diff - `archivist/snapshot.py` hashes all leaves into manifest-YYYYMMDD.json; --diff shows added/removed/modified since last snapshot. Verified: first two snapshots + a diff that catches a known edit.
10. External knowledge ingestion pipeline - `archivist/ingest.py` takes a research output (markdown or URL), extracts key facts, assigns provenance headers (source, date, confidence, TTL), writes into the correct leaf with index linkage; spec in memory/ops/ingestion-spec.md. Verified: 3 real research outputs processed end-to-end, each spot-checked against its source.

### Scribe — 10 goals
*theme: from per-round discipline-keeper to owner of automated, auditable memory infrastructure*
1. Decision trace API - every decision bullet carries one-line rationale + named owner + status + source citation, exposed via /api so any agent can trace "what did we decide about X" to the exact source. Verified: 100% of cycle-2 decisions queryable with resolvable source paths.
2. Contradiction detector - automated cross-check of a round's claims (numbers/sizes/hashes/counts) vs disk ground truth, flagging mismatches BEFORE they are recorded. Verified: seeding a false claim in a test run -> flagged pre-record.
3. Hot-file auto-trim + drift guard - tool enforcing MEMORY.md <40 lines with lossless archive, plus automatic MEMORY<->TODO goal-line drift detection each turn. Verified: forcing a 60-line MEMORY.md -> trimmed to <40 with moved content recoverable; a drift case caught same-turn.
4. Self-healing index / orphan sweep (coordinator role per charter) - schedule Archivist's index_check + memory_health runs every round so memory/INDEX.md stays a verified pointer map; baseline to beat: 324/441 orphans from cycle 1. Verified: weekly orphan-rate trend report showing monotonic improvement.
5. Supersession-chain integrity (policy owner per charter) - consume Archivist#5's validator output; enforce that every SUPERSEDED leaf points to its successor and the canonical head is unambiguous per topic; weekly run + report. Verified: cycle-2 weekly runs with zero unresolved heads.
6. Durable-copy guarantee - rule + check that every record Scribe lands in shared docs also gets a same-turn-indexed copy in memory/, so a sync-clobber can never lose Scribe's work again (direct fix for the recurring 11-13 clobber bug). Verified: audit of all cycle-2 Scribe artifacts -> 100% have durable copies.
7. Owner-coverage ledger with API - standing map of every open TODO item -> exactly one named owner, /api-exposed with per-round "newly unowned" delta; legacy FUTURE backlog quarantined and counted separately. Verified: endpoint returns 0 unowned at cycle-2 kickoff.
8. Round-record template + auto-synthesis - canonical decided/open/owner schema + a script that drafts the skeleton from turn evidence so compression is review-and-fill, not from-scratch. Verified: next round's record drafted by script with >=80% of fields pre-filled correctly.
9. Fleet memory-health dashboard - extend goal-dashboard.html with hot-file line count, orphan rate, contradiction count, supersession validity, owner-coverage %, durable-copy integrity (consumes Archivist#2 + Scribe#1/#4). Verified: dashboard renders all six metrics live from the API.
10. Compression quality gate (auto-lint) - 100% of bullets cite a source, 100% contradiction-checked, exact names/numbers/paths verbatim; automated lint on Scribe output before recording, pass/fail logged to the evidence ledger. Verified: one deliberately bad bullet rejected by the lint with the reason named.



